# What the image build must not carry.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` sends the whole working tree — including `target/`,
# which is several gigabytes of host-architecture build output that the builder
# stage cannot use and would rebuild anyway. The first attempt at this image
# failed with "no space left on device" while writing `target/debug/deps` into a
# layer, which is the clearest possible statement of the problem.

# Build output, host-architecture and useless in a container.
target/

# Built front ends. The image builds its own, from source, at a pinned
# toolchain; a dist/ copied from a laptop is a binary of unknown provenance.
examples/*/dist/

# Local runtime state: logs, the development database, and the shell's signing
# key. The key especially — it is the private half of what platforms verify
# tokens against, and it has no business in an image.
demo/state/

# Version control and editor leavings.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Browser tests and their downloaded browser.
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/screenshots/
e2e/report/
e2e/results/

# Python bytecode from the angreal tasks.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Documentation output.
site/
docs/api/

# Nothing here is read at build time.
.metis/
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
